  "answer_text": "# \ud83d\udcca Grade to Percentage Calculator\n\nHere is a complete guide and reference chart to convert grades to percentages (and vice versa).\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd22 How to Calculate Percentage from a Score\n\n\n1. **Add up** the number of points you earned on the test.\n2. **Divide** the points earned by the total points available.\n3. **Multiply** the result by **100** to get your percentage score.\n\n\n### Formula:\n> **Percentage = (Points Earned \u00f7 Total Points) \u00d7 100**\n\n**Example:** If you scored 45 out of 50:\n> (45 \u00f7 50) \u00d7 100 = **90%**\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccb Letter Grade to Percentage Conversion Chart\n\nHere is the standard grading scale used for letter grades:\n\n| Letter Grade | Percentage Range | GPA |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A+** | 97\u2013100% | 4.0 |\n| **A** | 93\u201396% | 4.0 |\n| **A\u2212** | 90\u201392% | 3.7 |\n| **B+** | 87\u201389% | 3.3 |\n| **B** | 83\u201386% | 3.0 |\n| **B\u2212** | 80\u201382% | 2.7 |\n| **C+** | 77\u201379% | 2.3 |\n| **C** | 73\u201376% | 2.0 |\n| **C\u2212** | 70\u201372% | 1.7 |\n| **D+** | 67\u201369% | 1.3 |\n| **D** | 63\u201366% | 1.0 |\n| **D\u2212** | 60\u201362% | 0.7 |\n| **F** | Below 60% | 0.0 |\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccc Simple (No +/\u2212) Grading Scale\n\nA typical straight-letter scale uses: **A = 90\u2013100**, **B = 80\u201389**, **C = 70\u201379**, **D = 60\u201369**, and **F = below 60**.\n\n| Letter Grade | Percentage Range |\n|---|---|\n| **A** | 90\u2013100% |\n| **B** | 80\u201389% |\n| **C** | 70\u201379% |\n| **D** | 60\u201369% |\n| **F** | Below 60% |\n\n---\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f Important Notes\n\n- Grading may vary among schools, classes, and teachers. Always check beforehand which system is used in your case.\n- The biggest mistake people make with grade converters is assuming that every school uses the same chart. That would make things easy, but it is not how grading works in real life. The standard U.S. plus/minus chart is common, yet it is still only one model.\n- Sometimes the border of a passing score is not 60%, but, e.g., 50 or 65%.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddee Quick Examples\n\n| Score | Total | Calculation | Percentage | Grade |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 45 | 50 | 45/50 \u00d7 100 | **90%** | A\u2212 |\n| 72 | 90 | 72/90 \u00d7 100 | **80%** | B\u2212 |\n| 35 | 60 | 35/60 \u00d7 100 | **58.3%** | F |\n| 18 | 25 | 18/25 \u00d7 100 | **72%** | C |\n\nWould you like me to calculate a specific score for you? Just provide your **points earned** and **total points**! \ud83c\udf93",
